#1512
A Bend in the Path~
   The path turns here between two fields that have not been ploughed in a
long while, though the old furrows can still be made out under the weeds.  A
pollarded tree stands at the corner with a length of rusted chain about its
trunk, and crows sit in it in a silence that has nothing to do with the hour.
~
