#1514
A Narrow Lane Between Hedgerows~
   Hedgerows close in on the path here, higher than your head and thick
enough to shut out the fields, and the way between them is worn to bare
earth.  A gate hangs from one hinge in the western hedge, and the gap it was
meant to close has been walked through so often the mud has turned to stone.
~
