E
hearth ash fire-basket~
   The ash in the hearth has been raked out and left in a neat pile on the
stone beside it, and the fire-basket within is empty and clean.  Someone shut
this house up carefully, and that is somehow worse than if they had left in a
hurry.
~
S
#1517
The Attic~
   The attic is low, and you must walk with your head bent.  Trunks and
bundles stand along the eaves under dust, strings of dried herbs hang from
the rafters, and a child's hoop lies toppled in the middle of the floor.  A
small window at the north end looks out toward the church.
~
