0 0 1516
E
marks tallies rafters wood~
   Under the highest of the rafters, where the light from the window just
reaches, small marks have been cut into the wood, a long row of them.  They
are not letters; they are only tallies, five and then a stroke across, kept
by somebody who counted a great many nights in this room.
~
S
#1518
A Paved Lane~
   The lane here is paved with round stones laid in the days when somebody
still minded such things, and the weeds have taken every joint between them.
The houses on either side stand with their shutters closed and their doors
barred, and not one chimney of the six above the roofs is giving out smoke.
~
