0 0 1520
E
fountain water slime stub~
   The fountain has been dry for longer than anyone now living in the village
can remember.  Its basin still holds a little of what rain gets past the
cracks, green and still and stinking faintly, and no bird of any kind has
been near it.
~
E
cross market steps mark~
   The market cross stands on three worn steps and carries no cross at all,
only the stump of its shaft, broken off low and long ago.  Upon the middle
step a mark has been drawn in something dark and greasy, a circle with a line
driven through it, and the rain has not managed to take it off.
~
S
#1520
The Old Well~
   A well of grey stone stands where the square narrows to a lane again, its
windlass seized and its bucket lying on its side in the weeds.  The rope that
should have been in the well has been cut, and the cut end hangs down into
the dark, where you can hear water a very long way down.
~
